## CURRENCY FORMATTING

Always use the `CurrencyFormatter` utility:
```dart
// GHS display
CurrencyFormatter.formatGhs(amount) // → "GHS 105,998"
// USD display
CurrencyFormatter.formatUsd(amount) // → "$4,200"
// With exchange rate conversion
CurrencyFormatter.ghsToUsd(amountGhs, rate) // → double
CurrencyFormatter.usdToGhs(amountUsd, rate) // → double
```

Never hardcode exchange rates. Always fetch from:
```dart
final rate = ref.watch(exchangeRateProvider).value?.usdToGhs ?? 15.40;
```


## SECURITY

Never generate, modify, or suggest changes to:
- firebase_options.dart
- google-services.json
- GoogleService-Info.plist
- .env files
- Any file containing API keys, secrets, or credentials

These are configured manually outside of Cursor.

---

## TESTING RULES

- Unit tests for all use cases (domain layer)
- Unit tests for all repository implementations (with mock data sources)
- Widget tests for critical screens (payment, bid outcome)
- Integration tests for auth flow
- Use `mocktail` for mocking
- Test files in `test/` mirroring `lib/` structure

---

## DO NOT

- Do NOT call Firestore directly from presentation layer (screens/notifiers)
- Do NOT import Firebase packages in domain layer
- Do NOT hardcode Firestore collection names as strings (use FirestoreCollections constants)
- Do NOT hardcode exchange rates
- Do NOT use get_it or injectable (Riverpod only for DI)
- Do NOT use Provider package (Riverpod only)
- Do NOT create global chat or document screens (these are per-order)
- Do NOT allow buyers to create payment requests
- Do NOT allow edit/cancel when firstPaymentMade = true (enforce in both UI and use case)
- Do NOT use `setState` in screens that have Riverpod providers
- Do NOT put business logic in widgets

